    "q-93419": {
      "dom_id": "step-q93419",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Which of the following is **not** the net of a prism?",
      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/d9010650127d8dcfcd387df09b9dce689ece90e3912ede882241c8b714f91d45.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIf we were to fold the net along its edges to form a solid shape, we'd get a triangular pyramid.\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/6bf9ac2bd130fdad3a056d0e5680e010003366f115e3655de59bbd795d1513f5.png)\n\nSo, the net that does not correspond to a prism is:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/f5be9bb97784c25d555d4581bc67916ab0b8e57ade33619b3df27d2eb0f59db2.png)\n\nThe rest of the given nets will give us a (triangular or rectangular) prism.",
