      "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/e7017b17e88561231e151d48fe5337bc82d164639f785eda0b0b148c9ee80b37.png)\n\nIf we were to fold the net above along its edges, then we'd get a rectangular pyramid, as shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/5e32ef37ef2dae4c714afcb744820c8fb1cbbc3bd23f7347552b3a7bc73949bc.png)\n\nSo, the net that does not correspond to a prism is:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14248692/assets/c35316b772366403fca0d0ba030866a82ef0d7c411c2817aa7e1feffa894c96e.png)\n\n   \n\nThe rest of the given nets will give us a (triangular or rectangular) prism.",
